{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Who are they that shall go?</b> Pharaoh wanted their heads, their elders, and their officers to go — men designated by name. But Moses answered him that the sons and daughters too would go, <b>for it is a feast to HaShem</b>, and there is a commandment upon all of us to hold a feast before Him. Then Pharaoh was angered on account of the sons and daughters, and he said that he would not send the little ones under any circumstances, for they would not sacrifice; rather, he would send all the adult males for the sake of the feast he mentioned, and the little ones and women would remain."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:05:21.123013017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}